BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Myth & Archetype as seen through Poetry & Astrology
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T170000
UID:6a5eda868a9917634a5f60d8@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:We invite all to a fascinating afternoon with Diana and Brian 
 who will explore through the respective lenses of astrology and poetry\, v
 aluable insights offered by both myth and archetype\, for better clarity a
 nd resilience in today’s tumultuous world.\nThis event features Author a
 nd Astrologer Diana Badger discussing her book "\nDance of the Archetypes:
  How Astrology Informs our Lives and Connects Us to the Earth"\,\nand Auth
 or/Poet/Storyteller Brian R. Martens with his book\,\n"Merlin’s Wing"\, 
 Mythic Poems.\nThis event is free\, all donations gratefully invited. Sele
 cted readings from each presenter\, a storytelling with Brian\, then Q&A\,
  book sales & signing\n.\nRefreshments for sale. OCA’s facilities are ac
 cessible to people with disabilities.\nDance of the Archetypes\nby Diana B
 adger\nWhether you’re new to astrology or already immersed in its symbol
 ism\,\nDance of the Archetypes\nilluminates the zodiac in a refreshingly a
 ccessible way. With grounded wisdom\, Diana connects planetary cycles to t
 he Earth we depend on\, our emotional lives\, and our healing. This is a b
 eautifully integrative guide for readers seeking relevance\, connection\, 
 and purpose in rapidly changing times\, brought to life by the author’s 
 own striking photographs.\nFor the past 20 years\, Diana Badger has woven 
 together parallel careers as a counseling astrologer and a writer/editor\,
  while pursuing an ongoing commitment to inner work and spiritual practice
 . Rooted in a reverence for the natural world and informed by multiple wis
 dom traditions\, Diana’s work reflects a lifelong inquiry into the relat
 ionship between psyche\, cosmos\, and Earth. She currently devotes her tim
 e to her\nEarth Sky Journal\npodcast/writing\, her astrology practice\, te
 nding of her garden\, and adventures in local community.\nMerlin’s Wing\
 nby Brian Martens\nThis collection of poems is concerned with the “Human
  Condition” : Awareness\, Transformation\, and Deep Intuition. His poetr
 y resonates with yearning\, humor and intelligence in which he expresses h
 is love and admiration for the first people\, the ancestors\, animal\, hum
 an and plant. He asks these voices to speak through him in symbols\, rhyth
 ms and revelations to reveal the deep beauty\, tragedy\, and unknowable my
 stery that surrounds him.\nBrian R. Martens is an abstract Artist\, Poet\,
  Author\, Creativity Facilitator\, International Speaker\, Myth Maker\, CA
  Poets in the Schools Instructor\, Podcaster\, and Storyteller. Brian weav
 es poetry\, myth\, and reflection into all his storytelling. His first boo
 k\,\nThree Raven Gate\n\, is a collection of haiku\, the form he learned f
 rom his work with Angeles Arrien Ph.D.\, a cross-cultural anthropologist\,
  over the course of seven years. Brian seeks to inspire and motivate peopl
 e\, with articles\, podcasts\, creativity workshops\, and poetry to recogn
 ize their own deep creative spirit and to express that to the world.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/myth-archet
 ype-as-seen-through-poetry-astrology
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Occidental Jazz Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T210000
UID:69b9822688b9754213a22729@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the inaugural Occidental Jazz Festival! Enjoy indo
 or and outdoor stages and great contemporary Jazz music at Occidental Cent
 er for the Arts. Delight in the sounds of amazing music\, the sights of ou
 r tranquil setting and the feeling of a warm and welcoming community.\nLin
 eup:\nFriday September 18th\n7-930 PM Glass Brick Boulevard (indoors)\nSat
 urday September 19th\n1:00 - 2 :40 PM Paul Hanson\, Michael Manring and Sc
 ott Amendola (outdoors)\n2:00 - 3:40 PM Ken Cook Trio (indoors)\n4:00 -4:4
 0 PM Junior Jazz All-Stars (outdoors)\n5:00 - 6:40PM Jaycie Grady 4Tet (ou
 tdoors)\n7:00 - 9:00 PM Jose Neto and Netoband (indoors)\nChoose your adve
 nture! Separate tickets are available for Friday night\, Saturday afternoo
 n (1-6:40 PM) or Saturday day & night (1-9 PM). Discounts for OCA members.
 \nWine\, beer\, refreshments and food available on-site or in downtown Occ
 idental (2 blocks away).\nKids 12 and under free. Free parking\, no dogs a
 llowed. Accessible to people with disabilities. Bring your own seat cushio
 n or low-backed chair for the amphitheater.\nTicket prices:\nFriday night 
 Glass Brick Boulevard $35\nSaturday afternoon only 1-6:40 PM $40\nSaturday
  afternoon & evening (with Netoband) $70\nGet Tickets\nPlease note\n: To a
 ttend Friday and Saturday you will need to make two ticket purchases - one
  for each date.\nDoors open at 6PM Friday September 18 and 12:00 PM Saturd
 ay September 19th.\nAbout the musicians:\nJose Neto and Netoband\nWorld-cl
 ass guitarist\nJosé Neto\nand his band\,\nthe Netoband\n\, have been perf
 orming together for over 25 years. For the last 18 years\, Neto has also b
 een touring internationally as Steve Winwood’s guitarist\, collaborating
  on numerous songs and projects together. Neto’s life and diverse musica
 l journey from Brazil to the United States and England was the subject of 
 the award-winning documentary\,\nThe Man Behind the White Guitar\n\, which
  was released to international film festivals in 2019.\nThe Netoband featu
 res Frank Martin – piano\, Celso Alberti – drums\, José Neto – guit
 ar\, Gary Brown – bass.\nGlass Brick Boulevard\nCreated in 1991\,\nGreg 
 Johnson\nand\nGlass Brick Boulevard\nrose to acclaim in the Bay Area in th
 e late ‘90s. Now reunited after a hiatus\, they’re making soul-soothin
 g music once again and inspiring audiences the world over. Led by their co
 mposer-pianist Johnson\, the band draws on a diverse array of influences\,
  including gospel\, Beethoven\, The Who\, and Motown\, to name just a few.
  Says Johnson\, “If Beethoven came back as Seal\, we'd be his band.” G
 lass Brick Boulevard is\nGreg Johnson on Piano\, Paul Hanson on Bassoon\, 
 Rob Fordyce on Bass and Celso Alberti on Drums.\nKen Cook Trio\nKen Cook\n
 - Pianist\, educator\, composer\nCalifornian native Ken Cook spent close t
 o twenty-five years on the east coast free lancing\, touring\, recording a
 nd teaching. He has performed in Europe\, Latin and South America and much
  of the Eastern United states with various groups including the great New 
 Orleans singer Johnny Adams. Currently based in the SF Bay Area\, he perfo
 rms often with his Jazz trio and can be found backing many other west coas
 t musicians. His music is a blend of Modern Jazz\, Soul\, Blues\, Latin an
 d Brazilian music. He has performed with Brazilian guitarist Ricardo Peixo
 to\, Blues singer Terrie Odabi\, cellist Mark Summer (Turtle Island String
  Quartet). He holds a Masters degree in Jazz Performance from the New Engl
 and Conservatory in Boston and is an alum of The Berklee College of Music 
 in Boston. He is an active clinician and educator and currently holds the 
 Jazz piano chair in the Jazz Studies Department at Sonoma State University
  in Rohnert Park\, CA.\nThe Ken Cook Trio includes\nMichael Pinkham\non ba
 ss and\nKendrick Freeman\non drums.\nJaycie Grady 4Tet\nThe Jaycie Grady 4
 Tet\nis a San Francisco-based jazz ensemble led by drummer J\naycie (JC) G
 rady\n. Primarily playing contemporary jazz\, their style is rooted in tra
 ditional jazz fundamentals but incorporates modern elements and diverse in
 strumentation\, such as the violin. JC was featured recently in the San Fr
 ancisco\nWomen in Jazz\nevent.\nHanson\, Manring & Amendola\nBass virtuoso
  Michael Manring is joined by fellow master Scott Amendola and Paul Hanson
  on electric bassoon. Get ready for an ensemble like you've never heard be
 fore!\nPaul Hanson\nhas recorded and/or performed with Grammy winners Bela
  Fleck and the Flecktones\, Jon Batiste\, Wayne Shorter and Taylor Eigsti.
  He has also recorded/ toured with Billy Cobham’s Crosswinds Ensemble\, 
 Peter Erskine\, Billy Childs\, Harmonica virtuoso Gregorie Maret\, Billy H
 iggins\, David Binney\, Ray Charles\, Charlie Hunter\, Patrice Rushen\, Al
 ex Acuna\, Dennis Chambers\, Abraham Laboriel\, Medeski Martin & Wood\, Bo
 b Weir’s RATDOG\, T. Lavitz from Dixie Dregs\, Jeff Coffin\, Jeff Sipe\,
  Jonas Hellborg\, Afro/Cuban pianist Omar Sosa\, Bob Moses\, Kai Eckhardt\
 , Peter Apfelbaum and the Hieroglyphics Ensemble\, 60string bassist Ariane
  Cap in the group OoN\, The Paul Dresher Ensemble\, DAVKA\, St. Joseph Bal
 let Company\, The Klezmorim\, as jazz soloist with the Oakland Eastbay Sym
 phony Orchestra\, as classical soloist with the Napa Symphony Orchestra (n
 on-improvising) and many more.\nMichael Manring\nis an acclaimed American 
 fretless bass virtuoso renowned for revolutionizing solo bass playing thro
 ugh innovative techniques\, alternate tunings\, and his signature Zon Hype
 rbass. A protégé of Jaco Pastorius\, Manring has released multiple solo 
 albums\, including\nSoliloquy\nand\nSmall Moments\n\, and was named 1994 B
 assist of the Year by Bass Player Magazine.\nFor\nScott Amendola\n\, the d
 rum kit isn’t so much an instrument as a musical portal. As an ambitious
  composer\, savvy bandleader\, electronics explorer\, first-call accompani
 st and capaciously creative foil for some of the world’s most inventive 
 musicians\, Amendola applies his wide-ranging rhythmic virtuosity to a vas
 t array of settings. His closest musical associates include guitarists Cha
 rlie Hunter\, Nels Cline\, and Jeff Parker\, Hammond B-3 organist Wil Blad
 es\, violinist Jenny Scheinman\, saxophonist Phillip Greenlief\, clarineti
 st Ben Goldberg\, bassists Trevor Dunn\, and Todd Sickafoose\, players who
  have each forged a singular path within and beyond the realm of jazz.\nWh
 ile rooted in the San Francisco Bay Area scene\, Amendola has woven a dens
 e and far-reaching web of bandstand relationships that tie him to influent
 ial artists in jazz\, blues\, rock and new music. A potent creative cataly
 st\, the Berkeley-based drummer is the nexus for a disparate community of 
 musicians stretching from Los Angeles and Seattle to Chicago and New York.
  Whatever the context\, Amendola possesses a gift for twisting musical gen
 res in unexpected directions.\nOver a career spanning more than three deca
 des\, Amendola has forged deep ties across the country\, and throughout th
 e world. As an ambitious composer\, savvy bandleader\, electronics explore
 r\, first-call accompanist\, and capaciously creative foil for some of the
  world’s most inventive musicians\, Amendola applies his wide-ranging rh
 ythmic virtuosity to a vast array of settings.\nJunior Jazz All-Stars\nThe
  Junior Jazz All Starts are an extraordinary group of young music enthusia
 sts. This amazing ensemble is assembled and directed by Greg Johnson of Gl
 ass Brick Boulevard\, and mentored by Music Directors Casey Jones - Analy 
 High School\, Bennett Friedman - Santa Rosa Junior College\, and Gary Jone
 s - Marin School of the Arts. Coming from a variety of musical backgrounds
 \, they forage a cool\, contemporary jazz sound. For the inaugural Jazz Fe
 stival they’re putting their own stamp on a few familiar Glass Brick Bou
 levard compositions.\nThe Junior Jazz All Stars are Julian Nelson on guita
 r\, Julia Busci on drums\, Robbie Paterson on Keyboards\, James Paterson o
 n Bass\, Choegyal Hergenrather on Soprano and Alto Sax\, and Songsten Herg
 enrather on Tenor Sax.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/tljb0twlk94
 yppdsibl7h1otstuq0z
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
